      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In rats which were injected with horseradish peroxidase (HRP) into the midbrain periaqueductal gray (PAG) and then administered with formaldehyde into the stomach, Fos-like immunoreactivity was found in tyrosine hydroxylase-like immunoreactive neurons in the nucleus tractus solitarii (NTS) which were retrogradely labeled with HRP. The results indicate that catecholaminergic NTS neurons may mediate nociceptive visceral information to the PAG."},
